rImages/450b670d-1295-4285-9665-369d26d94752.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /><img src=\"https://cdn-wl-assets.classplus.co/production/single/vlvkc/04254bd5-3730-4db2-9fba-adc9289f1cf9.jpeg\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"6","high":"6"},"solution":"<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/4a426d9b-7a9d-4093-a727-5792beacc57e.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Computer Science Engineer"},{"qnum":27,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/91feea2c-cdba-48b6-95c8-904fed70da95.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<p>a</p>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<p>b</p>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<p>c</p>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<p>d</p>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/f6a4536b-ad6f-4a98-afb0-2e77db43aa13.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Computer Science Engineer"},{"qnum":28,"type":"MSQ","correct":"A","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/72a0f18a-f510-4535-bd37-777c381519bb.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<p>a</p>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<p>b</p>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<p>c</p>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<p>d</p>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/965927e3-88e9-4576-a690-ca37ac4bc8ae.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Computer Science Engineer"},{"qnum":29,"type":"NAT","correct":"13","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/f06d7456-c06f-4e5a-83c4-6271b6474d3b.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /><img src=\"https://cdn-wl-assets.classplus.co/production/single/vlvkc/04254bd5-3730-4db2-9fba-adc9289f1cf9.jpeg\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"13","high":"13"},"solution":"<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/b2f0502f-895b-4659-9e43-758fd6dd75ba.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Computer Science Engineer"},{"qnum":30,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/0ea6c143-e7f9-4b72-897e-a2d3fbc0a02c.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<p>a</p>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<p>b</p>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<p>c</p>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<p>d</p>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><span>S &rarr; Aa | bAc | dc | bda</span><br /><span> A &rarr; d</span></p>\n<p><span>It is <strong>NOT LR(0)</strong> and <strong>NOT SLR(1)</strong>.</span></p>\n<p><span>Why NOT LR(0)</span><br /><span> In the initial LR(0) closure, because of <code>S &rarr; .Aa</code>, we also get <code>A &rarr; .d</code>. Also we have <code>S &rarr; .dc</code>.</span><br /><span> So on input <code>d</code>, we reach a state that contains both:</span></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><span><code>A &rarr; d .</code> (reduce item)</span></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span><code>S &rarr; d . c</code> (shift item on <code>c</code>)</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p><span>LR(0) would want to <strong>reduce</strong> (without lookahead) and also <strong>shift</strong> on <code>c</code> &rarr; <strong>shift/reduce conflict</strong>.</span></p>\n<p><span>Why NOT SLR(1)</span><br /><span> For SLR(1), reduce <code>A &rarr; d</code> only on FOLLOW(A).</span></p>\n<p><span>FOLLOW(A):</span></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><span>From <code>S &rarr; A a</code> &rArr; <code>a &isin; FOLLOW(A)</code></span></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span>From <code>S &rarr; b A c</code> &rArr; <code>c &isin; FOLLOW(A)</code></span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p><span>So <strong>FOLLOW(A) = { a, c }</strong>.</span></p>\n<p><span>In the same conflicting state, shift is on <code>c</code>, and because <code>c &isin; FOLLOW(A)</code>, SLR(1) also places the reduce on <code>c</code>. Conflict remains.</span></p>\n<p></p>\n<p><span>Final answer: <strong>(d) G is neither LR(0) nor SLR(1)</strong></span></p>","subject":"Computer Science Engineer"},{"qnum":31,"type":"NAT","correct":"75","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/9178bff8-7c42-4110-8cf8-38f20560733a.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /><img src=\"https://cdn-wl-assets.classplus.co/production/single/vlvkc/04254bd5-3730-4db2-9fba-adc9289f1cf9.jpeg\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"75","high":"75"},"solution":"<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/8d1f0d6f-0205-4047-ae67-bed2cebcbe8e.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Computer Science Engineer"},{"qnum":32,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/6f1f43c5-d6d3-446d-a03f-1055e1887650.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<p>a</p>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<p>b</p>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<p>c</p>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<p>d</p>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/2eb29c7c-13ec-433a-a71d-fa02661f33f7.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Computer Science Engineer"},{"qnum":33,"type":"NAT","correct":"66","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/d3f658c6-633e-4828-8be5-b1632ed919d6.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /><img src=\"https://cdn-wl-assets.classplus.co/production/single/vlvkc/04254bd5-3730-4db2-9fba-adc9289f1cf9.jpeg\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"66","high":"66"},"solution":"<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/0e9a4019-7dc4-4366-9502-2d3f51a4f748.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Computer Science Engineer"},{"qnum":34,"type":"NAT","correct":"4","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/7cd3627f-49da-4317-8178-9ed3de7536cc.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /><img src=\"https://cdn-wl-assets.classplus.co/production/single/vlvkc/04254bd5-3730-4db2-9fba-adc9289f1cf9.jpeg\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"4","high":"4"},"solution":"<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/036e3fdd-460b-45da-8ee5-35e0bf08cceb.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Computer Science Engineer"},{"qnum":35,"type":"NAT","correct":"3","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/82ec804e-f7e1-49e4-a4b7-dd3c0fd055a3.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /><img src=\"https://cdn-wl-assets.classplus.co/production/single/vlvkc/04254bd5-3730-4db2-9fba-adc9289f1cf9.jpeg\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"3","high":"3"},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/a9f36e8e1db5b6e7076361764dee094e3a16aa40.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Computer Science Engineer"},{"qnum":36,"type":"NAT","correct":"8","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/af0f279a-c94b-4ecc-b2f7-6463339732b7.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /><img src=\"https://cdn-wl-assets.classplus.co/production/single/vlvkc/04254bd5-3730-4db2-9fba-adc9289f1cf9.jpeg\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"8","high":"8"},"solution":"<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/4c7eafe4-0456-4e08-bcb1-1c3cb0bdda84.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/dabff824-570c-4739-9cff-e98c8b84defc.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Computer Science Engineer"},{"qnum":37,"type":"MSQ","correct":"B,C,D","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/f4a00d8e-9bf5-4909-829d-833f8bd48ee0.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<p>a</p>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<p>b</p>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<p>c</p>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<p>d</p>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p> Answer: (b), (c) and (d).</p>\n<p>Solution:</p>\n<p>First classify the transactions with respect to the checkpoint at t₁ and the crash at t₂:</p>\n<p>&bull; T1: started and committed before the checkpoint.</p>\n<p>&bull; T3: started before t₁, committed after t₁ but before t₂.</p>\n<p>&bull; T2: started after t₁, committed before t₂.</p>\n<p>&bull; T4, T5: not committed when the crash occurs at t₂.</p>\n<p>With immediate database modification and a simple checkpointing protocol:</p>\n<p>&bull; Transactions committed before the checkpoint (T1) neither need UNDO nor REDO.</p>\n<p>&bull; Transactions committed after the checkpoint but before the crash (T2, T3) must be REDO-ne to ensure their effects are on disk. REDO is done by scanning the log forward.</p>\n<p>&bull; Transactions active at the time of crash (T4, T5) must be UNDO-ne, scanning the log backward.</p>\n<p>&bull; The typical order is UNDO first, then REDO, not the other way around.</p>\n<p>Now check the options:</p>\n<p>(a) T1, T2, T3 redone in the forward direction &ndash; wrong transactions list (T1 is not redone).</p>\n<p>(b) T4, T5 undone in the forward direction &ndash; correct.</p>\n<p>(c) First UNDO then REDO &ndash; correct.</p>\n<p>(d) Transactions committed before the checkpoint (T1) neither need UNDO nor REDO &ndash; correct.</p>\n<p>So, the correct statement is:</p>\n<p>(b), (c) and (d).</p>\n<p></p>","subject":"Computer Science Engineer"},{"qnum":38,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/baa43893-16de-4af2-8faf-a3c78e88d21b.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<p>a</p>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<p>b</p>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<p>c</p>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<p>d</p>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/70742acc-4845-455f-a8aa-21e8d661d9a2.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Computer Science Engineer"},{"qnum":39,"type":"NAT","correct":"18","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/e8e75963-e07e-4631-8244-92117e406d83.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /><img src=\"https://cdn-wl-assets.classplus.co/production/single/vlvkc/04254bd5-3730-4db2-9fba-adc9289f1cf9.jpeg\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"18","high":"18"},"solution":"<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/7fe76531-ac62-4976-b6b7-1aec176e8726.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Computer Science Engineer"},{"qnum":40,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/740bbc59-2d9b-485b-ad97-0cb8eceec093.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<p>a</p>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<p>b</p>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<p>c</p>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<p>d</p>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/8c92a829-8aa6-41a3-a57d-0c02baf6a1ad.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Computer Science Engineer"},{"qnum":41,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/4fefd38f-1067-49ce-b34f-0f341de216fa.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<p>a</p>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<p>b</p>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<p>c</p>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<p>d</p>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"